  "label": "the scenario of having a pet is presented as a substitute for human interaction",
  "description": "The text 'when you've got a loyal animal companion' is mapped onto the visual material of the couple in bed, suggesting that the presence of a pet (implied by the text) is sufficient to fulfill the emotional needs that human interaction would otherwise provide. The visual scene of the couple is used to represent the context in which this substitution is being proposed.",
